<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 61,592 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 61,592 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 61,592 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Saturday compared to 144,268 tonnes in the same period on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Saturday    March 7</p>
<p>    Export cargo		23,297	29,302</p>
<p>    Import cargo		38,295     114,966</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, 12 ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight are expected to sail and 10 to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs     Ship		 Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 60,00	     Miraj		9/3</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	    Wawasen Megah    8/3</p>
<p>High speed diesel    75,660	    Chesapeake City  11/3</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     22,649	    Seram		8/3</p>
<p>Phosphate		29,887	    Lapanto Glory    20/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
